Subject: [PATCH] tests: client-eviction: wait for the query buffer and the eviction

Backport to redis 7.0.15 of the two upstream hunks that fix the race in
tests/unit/client-eviction.tcl "client evicted due to percentage of
maxmemory" (the test writes a query on one connection and immediately checks
CLIENT LIST on another; the server may not have read the bytes yet, so the
qbuf / eviction check can run too early; the failed test also leaves
maxmemory 6mb set, which evicts the next test's client):

- redis/redis 447ce11a64bbcb79b0336a0940c2fb62993e7586
  "solve race conditions in tests (#13433)", Oran Agra, 2024-07-22:
  wait_for_condition before the tot-mem check.
- redis/redis 64a40b20d906f019a32fcb227c938768079dd9ed
  "Async IO Threads (#13695)", Yuan Wang, 2024-12-23 (test hunk only):
  `assert {![client_exists $cname]}` -> wait_for_condition.

The hunks are taken verbatim; only the context is 7.0.15's. The other
client-eviction.tcl hunks of 64a40b20 are about io-threads (not in 7.0) and
are not backported. Applied by scripts/mk-guest-rootfs.sh (KJIT K4).

--- a/tests/unit/client-eviction.tcl
+++ b/tests/unit/client-eviction.tcl
@@ -93,6 +93,11 @@
         set n [expr $maxmemory_clients_actual / 2]
         $rr write [join [list "*1\r\n\$$n\r\n" [string repeat v $n]] ""]
         $rr flush
+        wait_for_condition 100 10 {
+            [client_field $cname tot-mem] >= $n
+        } else {
+            fail "Failed to fill qbuf for test"
+        }
         set tot_mem [client_field $cname tot-mem]
         assert {$tot_mem >= $n && $tot_mem < $maxmemory_clients_actual}
         
@@ -103,7 +108,11 @@
             $rr write [join [list "*1\r\n\$$maxmemory_clients_actual\r\n" [string repeat v $maxmemory_clients_actual]] ""]
             $rr flush
         } e
-        assert {![client_exists $cname]}
+        wait_for_condition 100 10 {
+            ![client_exists $cname]
+        } else {
+            fail "Failed to evict client"
+        }
         $rr close
         
         # Restore settings
